ammist@athena.mit.edu (The Mist) writes:

>  What do I do at fountains?  I can hear naiads and coins and stuff, but I have
>no idea what to do when I get to the fountain.  I've tried invoking and applying.

You can 
 - drink from the fountain. Stand on it, and use the q command like you would
   drink a potion. There are various possible effects, some of them are good 
   and others aren't..
 - #dip an item to the fountain. It _may_ become uncursed if it was cursed.
   If you dip potions twice, they become potions of water. If you dip scrolls
   or spellbooks, they will become blank (again, after two dippings, i 
   suppose).

>  How can you tell if a creature is alligned a certaiain way?  And what sort of
>bodies should I sacrifice at an altar?

Usually all you have to know is whether it is peaceful or not. If you try
attacking a peaceful monster, the game asks if you really want to hit it.
Usually you don't want to hit peaceful monsters.

Sacrifice anything except humans and werecreatures (well, chaotic characters
can sacrifice these, too) and undead monsters (&,V,Z). If you're an elf, don't 
sacrifice elves.
And one more thing: the corpse you sacrifice, should be fresh. That is, it
shouldn't have been dead for a long time. Lizard corpses are an exception,
they stay fresh until they disintegrate or get eaten.
